#: rc.cpp:62 rc.cpp:235
msgid ""
"Here you can type a keyword or expression to be used for this filter which "
"depends on the condition you selected in the combo box at the right:<ul>\n"
"<li><b>contain</b>, <b>doesn't contain</b> - you should probably enter a "
"keyword here, like \"KDE\", \"Baseball\" or \"Business\". The keyword is not "
"case-sensitive so it doesn't matter whether you type \"kde\", \"KDE\" or "
"\"kDe\".</li>\n"
"<li><b>equals</b>, <b>doesn't equal</b> - enter a phrase or expression here "
"to have the filter match only those articles whose headlines match "
"<b>exactly</b>"
" the text you typed. The phrase you type will be considered to be "
"case-sensitive, so it makes a difference whether you show articles which "
"contain \"Boeing\" or \"BOEING\".</li>\n"
"<li><b>matches</b> - a regular expression is expected. Recommended only if "
"you are familiar with regular expressions, i.e. it should be used by "
"advanced users only.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

